    {
      "id": "bs-did%3Aplc%3Akhkkkhl5yezvfymz4g4tnukt%2Fapp.bsky.feed.post%2F3n2hevlhfuc2f",
      "source": "bluesky",
      "published_at": "2026-11-16T20:35:14Z",
      "title": "#NBA Power Rankings, Week 5! ",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/johnschuhmann.bsky.social/post/3n2hevlhfuc2f",
      "author": "John Schuhmann",
      "thumbnail": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:khkkkhl5yezvfymz4g4tnukt/bafkreidcv5xdlpc6rzbkwhyyzb3l3w36yi6eksimxli6b2grhfnbikgccu",
      "body_excerpt": "#NBA Power Rankings, Week 5! \n\nFeaturing the usual notes & numbers...\n\nwww.nba.com/news/power-r...",
      "players": [],
      "teams": [],
      "media": {
        "type": "image",
        "images": [
          {
            "url": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:khkkkhl5yezvfymz4g4tnukt/bafkreidcv5xdlpc6rzbkwhyyzb3l3w36yi6eksimxli6b2grhfnbikgccu",
            "alt": "The Heat have won four straight games to climb above .500 for the first time. The first two wins came in Sacramento and Utah, but they then swept a back-to-back with the Cavs and Pistons over the weekend.\n\nTwo takeaways\n\nThe Heat scored 134 points per 100 possessions over the weekend back-to-back and now account for three of the 14 games where a team has scored at least 133 per 100. Giannis Antetokounmpo totaled 71 points in 62 minutes over the two games, with 55 of those 71 points coming in the restricted area (21-for-26) or the free throw line (13-for-20). He’s also now 22-for-41 (54%) from mid-range, the best mark among 27 players with at least 30 mid-range attempts and up 36% over his first 13 seasons.\n\nDavion Mitchell leads the league with 9.2 assists per game, having dished out 17 (with just one turnover) in the Heat’s win over Cleveland on Friday. He drives Miami’s transition game, also leading the league with 8.4 pass-ahead passes per game, and his 34 assists to Antetokounmpo are the most from any player to a single teammate.\n\nComing up: The remainder of the Heat’s five-game homestand features visits from the Rockets and Thunder. Oklahoma City has the league’s second paint defense and might test Antetokounmpo’s mid-range shooting on Sunday."
          }
        ]
      },
      "avatar": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:khkkkhl5yezvfymz4g4tnukt/bafkreigez4sk24rikgcjnq3qou3hpmtnvi3c5xi43ginkbmnd3s3s7qhgy",
